          <Description>"Keep scene audio after death (A1)"</Description>
          <VariableType>Auto Assembler Script</VariableType>
          <AssemblerScript>{ BH6 / RE6 - A1: skip the GameOver audio-mode request - TEST

  Purpose: keep death animations while testing continued scene audio.
  User confirmed continued audio after death on 2026-09-07.
  One scenario tested with the original Gemini patch enabled.
  Animation details and other death scenarios need further testing.

  Analyzed EXE SHA256:
  72B52D06A1C878A6D66701B192A47557BD844A0473D6F3CAFB0C736144235F74

  Site: BH6.exe+71B35, call BH6.exe+1374A0
  Callee: sets sBioSound mode 7 and two volume targets to zero.
  Only this call site is changed. No hook, timer, allocation or trace.

  Use either KEEP BLOOD or Gemini as the No Game Over option, never both.
  Disable other experimental GameOver patches. Enable A1 BEFORE death.
  Reload the checkpoint to restore an already-muted scene first.
  Disabling A1 restores code, not an already-changed audio state.
}

