          <AssemblerScript>{ BH6 / RE6 - B1: block common death BGM requests

  Targets: bgm0100.sngw through bgm0104.sngw.
  Current snd_cmn_bgm.stq IDs 1..5 reference source rows 0..4.
  The two verified callers below request only these IDs.
  bgm6666 (ID 6), other BGM tables and scene audio are unaffected.

  Analyzed EXE SHA256:
  72B52D06A1C878A6D66701B192A47557BD844A0473D6F3CAFB0C736144235F74

  BH6.exe+71B7B: ID 1 -&gt; common BGM wrapper +13BAB0.
  BH6.exe+5E69CD: ID 2/3/4/5 -&gt; same wrapper.
  The original callee uses RET 8. ADD ESP,8 replaces its stack cleanup.
  Both callers ignore its return value; no injected code is needed.

  Enable before the next death. Existing playback is not stopped.
  Keep A1 and the selected No Game Over option enabled.
  The five files must have their original names for a valid audio test.
  This entry never renames, deletes, or edits files.
  Gameplay verification is pending.
}

