        <CheatEntry>
          <ID>21919</ID>
          <Description>"GPT-6 NO GAME OVER - KEEP BLOOD EFFECT"</Description>
          <VariableType>Auto Assembler Script</VariableType>
          <AssemblerScript>{ RE6 / BH6 - GPT-6 NO GAME OVER + KEEP BLOOD EFFECT (STANDALONE TEST)

  This entry is independent. Do NOT enable it together with "No Game Over - Gemini".
  Revision 3: skip only uIdGameover00 menu initialization. All other sUnit
  objects, including death-demo and blood/effect objects, retain their original
  initialization. The resource table count is reduced from
  five to three so the two snd_sm1545 death-sound rows are not requested.

  Target build: BH6.exe SHA256
  72B52D06A1C878A6D66701B192A47557BD844A0473D6F3CAFB0C736144235F74
  Menu vtable: VA 01590F40; constructor writes it at BH6.exe+59CC2A.
  The old VA 0163FDD0 was a type-descriptor vtable, not a game-object vtable.
  Enable before death; an already-created menu requires a checkpoint reload.
  TEST: blood appearance and other death scenarios still require gameplay checks.
  The 4 KB code buffer is reused and retained until process exit so disabling
  cannot free code while a game thread is still returning from it.
}

[ENABLE]
// Original site: cmp ecx,1 / jne +57 / mov edx,[esi] / and eax,-6
 aobscanmodule(bh6_keep_blood_site,BH6.exe,75 57 8B 16 83 E0 FA 83 C8 02 89 46 10)
 assert(bh6_keep_blood_site,75 57 8B 16 83 E0 FA 83 C8 02)
